  "issues": [
    "No prices anywhere in the sheet; all priceUsd are null.",
    "MESRUBATLAR / SOFT DRINKS: rows such as 'SODA / MINERAL WATER' (followed by SAN PELLEGRINO, AYRAN, BRITVIC...) and 'MEYVE SUYU / FRUIT JUICE' are ambiguous heading-vs-item; kept all as flat items under Soft Drinks. SODA / MINERAL WATER may be a sub-heading for SAN PELLEGRINO, AYRAN, BRITVIC.",
    "BRITVIC flavour line 'TOMATO, BITTER LEMON, GINGER ALE, TONIC' is English only: put in detailEn, detailTr null.",
    "'SU / WATER 330 ml.' and 'SU CAM / WATER 330 ml.': the volume is printed only after the English part; tr='SU' / 'SU CAM', en='WATER 330 ml.' (volume not a price).",
    "'FRESH MEYVE SUYU/ FRESH FRUIT JUICE' is a separate top-level category in my output only because of its position? No: it is an item in Soft Drinks; it is placed after Soft Drinks items inside a list. Check below.",
    "Ronnefeldt tea bags: parenthetical notes in the Turkish part were moved from the name into detailTr (e.g. EARL GREY (bergamot) -> name EARL GREY, detailTr 'bergamot'). Original spelling/typos kept (PAPAPTYA, NENE, REFRESHING MINT with Turkish dotted I).",
    "Printed typos kept verbatim: APERATIFLER/APERATIVES, CAÇHACA, MILAGRA REPOSADO, GRANDE ABSENTH, DOM BENETICTINE, ANGUSTRA, 'INTERNATIONALS COCKTAILS', 'NENE YAPRAKLARI', 'PAPAPTYA'.",
    "Signature cocktails: only ILLUSION has both a Turkish and an English line (the two differ: EN omits chocolate bitter and says 'sour sauce'); PORT, THE PASSION, HARMONY, AURA have Turkish ingredients only (detailEn null). Cocktail names kept identical in tr and en.",
    "International cocktails have an English-only ingredient line (detailEn); detailTr null. Their recipes differ from the Whiskey Lounge cocktail sheet (e.g. OLD FASHIONED uses J.W. BLACK LABEL 12 Y.O. and walnut marmelade here, bourbon whiskey and sugar there).",
    "Hot drinks: 'ESPRESSO, RISTRETTO, LUNGO' is a single row (one item, not three).",
    "Lobby bar sheet gives no volumes (cl) for spirits."
  ]
